# Claude Code configuration, including the permission rules. It belongs to the user, not to this
# codebase, so formatting never rewrites it: a trailing newline added here is a diff on a security
# setting nobody asked for.
.claude/

# Build output and local state. Never formatted, and skipping them keeps pnpm format fast.
dist/
**/dist/
local-data/
coverage/

# The approved architecture specification, held here byte-identical to the document that was
# reviewed. It is a received artifact rather than this codebase's prose, and the whole point of the
# in-repo copy is that it is the same document; reformatting it would make "authoritative" ambiguous.
docs/architecture/
